# Marketplays — Backend / API

**Mechanics (source of truth):** `docs/marketplays_cursor_rules.md` **Section 5** (+ always **Sections 1–2**). Schema: **Section 4**. Deploy: **Section 2** / `docs/deployment.md`.

**Sequencing / priority:** `docs/marketplays_launch_roadmap.md` (Phase 1 MVP first; AI agents / Nice-to-Have out of scope until launch-ready). Doc map: `docs/COMPATIBILITY.md`.

**Auth:** Clerk per launch roadmap Conflicts — supersedes JWT/bcrypt bullets in rules Section 5.1 for *authentication provider only*. RBAC unchanged: gate buyer/seller/admin on every protected route (Clerk session/role claims replace JWT role claim).

## Entrypoint
- FastAPI instance named `app` in `apps/api/app/main.py` (Vercel: `[tool.vercel] entrypoint`)
- Fallback re-export: `apps/api/api/index.py`
- Crons in `apps/api/vercel.json`: booking transitions `1 0 * * *`, availability extend `0 0 * * *`

## Security (non-negotiable)
- Auth provider: **Clerk** (not custom JWT/bcrypt) — verify Clerk session / claims server-side
- Role middleware on every protected route (RBAC principle unchanged)
- Validate Stripe-Signature on all webhooks → 400 if invalid
- SQLAlchemy ORM only — never interpolate user input into SQL
- Auth/login abuse controls + uploads: MIME + size server-side

## Domain
- Booking transitions exactly as Section 5.2 — clients never PATCH `status` arbitrarily
- CIS formula Section 5.3; money = integer pence
- Filters: AND across types, OR within multi-select (Section 5.4)
- Long-running work stays off Vercel Functions (Section 2.3)
